  "campus": "Atlanta",
  "campus_description": "ATL@ONLINE",
  "course_description": "Industry seminar courses fall outside the scope of traditional academic coursework, and instead allow students to learn from and interact with experienced practitioners, and to develop industry-specific insights, fine-tune career skills, and increase professional exposure.",
  "course_notes": "The goal of the Applied Field Experience seminar is to enhance the value of an internship by helping each student apply what they learn in the classroom to the workplace. You will reflect on the internship experience to identify the skills you are building, the culture of that workplace, and the work you are doing to determine how these areas inform your career progression. The seminar is for students who will have an internship for the Fall or Spring semester only. The course is conducted through a virtual classroom and requires weekly responses and the submission of short essays. You can meet with the instructor in person or via Zoom to ask questions. In consultation with their academic advisors, BBA students in their final term in Goizueta are permitted to work up to 40 hours per week of they have a reduced course load of 1-11 credits. If you are an international student completing an internship in a Fall or Spring term this is the required course for CPT approval. Please contact Kim Timpone (ktimpon@emory.edu) in order to enroll in this seminar.",
